<h2 class="design">The man who walked away</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">Jimmy Moy, Chinese Laundryman</h4>

<p>

Michael Brick's <a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2005/11/18/nyregion/18gone.html">Tracing Steps Of The Man Who Walked Away</a>: He walked these avenues and then he was gone, as the inhabitants of one city give way to the next, as some are hurried along. Everyone leaves behind a name, a time, a place and a role, and his were Jimmy Moy, 1960, Park Slope, Brooklyn: the man who never returned.
