                            <a name="comment224"></a>
<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: The man who walked away
</h4>

<p>
Well, if you must know, when you put the story up I was home trying to clean up a story for Sunday. And I was trying way too hard to say what the story was about, to justify its existence. Anyway, reading this helped. I went straight from the last paragraph of the second reading back to my draft and cut a bunch of junk out. Not enough, but a lot. It's weird, because at times I can be pretty spare, but this guy is more. I think he's confusing at times. I think he can be too much of a certain thing. But he was so far in that direction it helped jerk me back toward the center. I could've gone farther. Maybe I should've read it three times.
</p>
